{{also|Kindergarten|kindergärten|Kindergärten}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|kindergarden}} {{qual|misspelling}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|de|Kindergarten|lit=garden of children||kindergarten}}, coined by German pedagogue Friedrich Fröbel (early 19th century); unrelated to {{m|en|kid}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US|CA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈkɪndəɹˌɡɑːɹt(ə)n/|/ˈkɪndəɹˌɡɑːɹd(ə)n/|[ˈkʰɪn(d)əɹˌɡɑːɹt̬(ə)n]|[ˈkʰɪɾ̃əɹˌɡɑːɹʔn̩]}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈkɪndəˌɡɑːt(ə)n/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑː(ɹ)tən}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|+|kindergärten|pl2qual=obsolete}}

# An educational institution for young children, usually between ages 4 and 6; [[nursery school]]. {{defdate|from 1852}}
# {{lb|en|US}} The [[elementary school]] [[grade]] before [[first grade]].
# {{lb|en|Philippines}} The two levels between [[nursery]] and [[prep]]; the second and third years of [[preschool]].

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|nursery school}}
* {{l|en|preschool}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|kindergartener}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|kindergartner}}

